Ambassador Dan Negrea
Representative of the United States to the UN Economic and Social Council
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President—and welcome Foreign Minister Rasmussen to the Council. Also, we’d like to welcome the presence of her excellency Ms. Melbārde, Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs of Latvia. And thank you to Under-Secretary-General DiCarlo and Fletcher for their briefings today.
I would like to use this opportunity to congratulate the people of Ukraine as they commemorate their 35th Independence Day. The United States remains committed to Ukraine’s future as a sovereign and prosperous nation.
We join President Trump in continuing to call for an immediate ceasefire and good-faith negotiations to end the Russia-Ukraine war and return peace and stability to both countries.
Deaths continue to mount, strike after strike. We call on both sides to end any strikes that target or risk damaging civilian vessels.
It is senseless to continue to spill blood of innocent civilians when there is no military solution to this war. Russia and Ukraine must return to the negotiating table.
The United States will play whatever constructive role, part, it can to facilitate talks between Moscow and Kyiv to achieve this outcome.
Thank you.
